  "body_markdown": "Skip to content\n\nDental Implants\n\nDental Implant Surgery\n\nAll-on-4 Dental Implants\n\nFixed Teeth vs. Removable\n\nCost & Compare\n\nDental Implant FAQ\n\nAesthetics\n\nCosmetic Dentistry\n\nPorcelain Veneers\n\nDental Crowns & Bridges\n\nSmile Makeover\n\nTeeth Whitening\n\nTreatments\n\nSedation Dentistry\n\nOral Surgery\n\nEmergency Dentistry\n\nConditions We Treat\n\nWhat To Expect\n\nPatient Center\n\nInsurance & Financing\n\nSmile Gallery\n\nWho We Are\n\nWhy Choose Us\n\nMeet Dr. Esam Nahlah\n\nMeet The Team\n\nVideo Library\n\nPatient Stories\n\nFor Doctors\n\nReferral Form\n\nContact Us\n\nBlog\n\nCurrent Patients\n\nTysons Corner: (703) 448-3312\n\nAlexandria: (703) 940-5410\n\nNew Patients\n\nTysons Corner: (571) 619-9442\n\nAlexandria: (571) 410-3430\n\nBook now\n\n\n## Book Now\n\n\n\n## Book Now\n\n\n\n## Uncovering the Mystery: The In-depth Guide to Dental Implants\n\n\nOctober 14, 2024\n\n\n#### Share This Post\n\n\nDental implants are not merely another restoration aesthetic but a fantastic solution for lost or damaged teeth. They assist in bridging the gap, providing both function and form. The technology behind them relies on a simple but elegant scientific concept- osseointegration. This is the physiological process where the implant integrates with the jawbone. Implant materials, often titanium, fuse with the bone, forming a stable foundation for replacement teeth, mimicking the functionality and feel of natural teeth.\n\n\n## Types of Dental Implants in McLean, VA\n\n\nThe most relevant to patients are endosteal and subperiosteal implants. Endosteal implants find their place in healthy jawbones, while subperiosteal implants rest above the jawbone beneath the gum tissue. Each presents unique advantages catering to different conditions and patients’ needs, though the best choice is always determined after a careful specialist examination.\n\nBoth options provide a durable, aesthetically pleasing outcome tailored to enhance the patient’s oral function and overall appearance. With advancements in dental technology, implants have become a highly successful and accessible treatment, restoring confidence and improving the quality of life for patients with missing teeth.\n\n\n## The Dental Implant Procedure: A Step-by-Step Guide\n\n\nThe dental implant procedure has multiple steps, from consultation to post-operative care. It begins with a thorough assessment, followed by implant placement and abutment connection. Throughout the procedure, it’s imperative to find a seasoned professional; a skilled hand lends itself to a more prosperous and comfortable experience.\n\nPost-operative care is just as critical as the procedure itself. Your dentist will provide detailed instructions on caring for your implant, including tips on maintaining good oral hygiene and managing discomfort during healing. Regular follow-up visits will ensure that the implant remains healthy and stable.\n\nOur skilled and experienced dentist can make all the difference in ensuring a smooth, successful procedure, reducing the risk of complications, and providing a more comfortable experience. Their expertise in surgical and restorative aspects of dental implants will help achieve a natural, durable result that enhances your smile and oral health for years.\n\n\n## Post-Implant Care: Making the Most out of Your Dental Implants\n\n\nBy maintaining good oral hygiene, the benefits of dental implants can last a lifetime. Running parallel to natural teeth care, dental implant care comprises regular brushing, flossing, and timely dental check-ups. A strong emphasis on overcoming unhealthy habits such as smoking or sugary diets further increases the longevity of the implants. Our services and procedures are deliberately shaped to provide a holistic experience, making your journey to a fantastic smile pleasant. With cutting-edge technology and certified skills, we deliver premier-grade dental implants, tending to each individual’s requirements.\n\n\n## Why Choose Us for Your Dental Implants?\n\n\nChoosing our practice gives patients access to world-class dental professionals who provide high-quality dental implant procedures with precision and care. Emphasizing patient comfort and care, we offer options tailored to each individual’s needs. We ensure that our patients get the best results and care possible.\n\nAre you ready to restore your smile with dental implants at our skilled and trusted dental practice? Please don’t wait to get the smile of your dreams with us. Please contact our doctors, Dr. Nahlah, and our exceptional team at our practice in McLean, VA, to schedule an appointment today!\n\nPrevPreviousUncover the Lifespan: How Long Can a Dental Implant Last?\n\nNextYour Comprehensive Guide on Dental Implants: The Best Replacement of Tooth SolutionNext\n\n\n#### More To Explore\n\n\n\n### Unlock the Benefits of Dental Implants: Your Best Teeth Replacement Option\n\n\nTooth loss can become an unfortunate reality for many as we age. Thankfully, advancements in dental technology, like dental implants,\n\nRead More »\n\nOctober 26, 2024\n\n\n### Your Comprehensive Guide on Dental Implants: The Best Replacement of Tooth Solution\n\n\nDental implants in McLean, VA are small, and titanium posts are surgically placed in your jawbone underneath your gum line.\n\nOctober 20, 2024\n\n\n## You Are Welcome Here.\n\n\nSchedule your consultation today.\n\nFacebook Instagram Youtube Google\n\n\n#### Contact Us\n\n\nAddresses:\n\nTysons Corner\n\n7901 Jones Branch Dr., Suite 220\n\nMcLean, VA 22102\n\nNew Patients: (571) 619-9442\n\nCurrent Patients: (703) 448-3312\n\nAlexandria\n\n2855 Duke St,\n\nAlexandria, VA 22314\n\nNew Patients: (571) 410-3430\n\nCurrent Patients: (703) 940-5410\n\n\n#### Hours\n\n\nMonday: 8:00am – 5:00pm\n\nTuesday: 8:00am – 5:00pm\n\nWednesday: 8:00am – 5:00pm\n\nThursday: 8:00am – 5:00pm\n\nFriday: 8:00am – 2:00pm\n\nSaturday: Closed\n\nSunday: Closed\n\n\n#### Services\n\n\nAll-On-4® Implants\n\nCrowns & Bridges\n\n\n#### About Us\n\n\nMeet the Doctor\n\nAbout Us\n\nBefore & After Photos\n\n2025 Dr. Nahlah. All rights reserved",
